NOTE ON DATA

The licence above covers this project's own source code. It does not cover the
data the map displays, which belongs to other people and keeps their terms.

The map stores no copy of any dataset. It requests them from the publisher when
someone opens the page. If you export a file from the app, or take a snapshot
with the optional script in scripts/, the terms below travel with whatever you
produced.

  CalEnviroScreen
    California Office of Environmental Health Hazard Assessment.
    Public State of California data. The state records the dataset as having
    no restrictions on public use. Cite OEHHA regardless.
    https://oehha.ca.gov/calenviroscreen

  EPA ECHO and the Facility Registry Service
    United States Environmental Protection Agency.
    Public domain federal data. Cite EPA.
    https://echo.epa.gov/

  OpenStreetMap
    (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the Open Database Licence
    (ODbL). Attribution is required, and the map displays it. If you
    redistribute geodata derived from it, you must share it alike.
    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

  Basemap tiles
    CARTO, built on OpenMapTiles and OpenStreetMap data. Attribution for all
    three is displayed on the map and must stay there.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NOTE ON WHAT THE OUTPUT IS

Some layers in this app are not data at all. The simulator, the modeled proxy
grid and the proximity index are computed by the app itself and describe no
real measurement. Files exported from those features are named and labelled to
say so, in the filename and inside the file.

Nothing in this project is a health risk assessment, a regulatory finding, or
evidence that any facility has caused harm. Redistributing an export does not
change that, and stripping the warnings out of one would be a misrepresentation
regardless of this licence.
